<title>USA: American ECO says agrees $58 mln placement.</title>
<headline>American ECO says agrees $58 mln placement.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON, Texas 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>American ECO Corp said on Friday it agreed a placement of up to $58 million worth of Canadian funds with underwriters Canaccord Capital Corp and Griffiths McBurney Partners of Toronto.</p>
<p>Under the proposed deal, special warrants would be convertible into common shares in order to close the previously announced acquisition of Ohio-based Chempower, the company said in a statement.  </p>
<p>Chempower was being acquired via a cash merger. Funds would be held in escrow until the merger was approved by shareholders, American ECO said.</p>
<p>Chempower is a manufacturing, construction and environmental services company for the power generation industry in 14 eastern United States.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
